# Known findings for scripts/check-template-directives.sh, deferred rather than
# suppressed. Each record names the issue that will close it.
#
# Format, tab-separated, five fields:
#
#   <rule>  <template>  <subject>  <issue>  <reason>
#
#   rule      unguarded-evidence | state-file-read
#   template  repository-relative path
#   subject   state name for unguarded-evidence, gate name for state-file-read
#   issue     owner/repo#N -- required; a record without one is an error
#   reason    why it is deferred rather than fixed
#
# Blank lines and #-comments are ignored. The check reads this file, so a
# record landing here is a deliberate, dated decision rather than a silence.
#
# Why these four are deferred and not fixed in the same change that introduces
# the check: all four are behaviour changes to shipped skills. Putting a when
# clause on work-on.md's research state changes when a /work-on run stops for
# the agent, and the three execute.md escalate states each need a decision
# about what the guard keys on before the failure_reason they assemble is
# worth anything. That is separate work from landing the lint, and a lint that
# cannot land until the defects it finds are fixed does not land.

unguarded-evidence	skills/work-on/koto-templates/work-on.md	research	tsukumogami/shirabe#333	The research state is silently skipped: koto advances through it on entry, so the directive asking for codebase research never reaches the agent and context_gathered is never submitted. Fixing it changes a shipped skill's behaviour and belongs in its own change.
unguarded-evidence	skills/execute/koto-templates/execute.md	escalate	tsukumogami/koto#202	Collects failure_reason for the batch view and hands it to done_blocked through a context assignment. Unguarded, so the state advances before the agent supplies it and the assignment interpolates an empty value.
unguarded-evidence	skills/execute/koto-templates/execute.md	escalate_dirty_merge_state	tsukumogami/koto#202	Same shape: accepts a rationale naming the conflict files for the operator, then assigns it into failure_reason. The operator-facing text is lost for the same reason.
unguarded-evidence	skills/execute/koto-templates/execute.md	escalate_upstream_drift	tsukumogami/koto#202	Same shape: accepts a rationale for why the upstream change invalidates the chain's intent, then assigns it into failure_reason.
